[2026-06-26] REVIEW: System Stabilization — ALL 10 BUGS FIXED

## Bugs fixed

### Bug 1 — CentralLogger triggers orchestrator (logs→orchestration loop)
Fix: CentralLogger is append-only async. Never writes to state. Never calls orchestration methods.

### Bug 2 — StateManager writes on every set (re-index storm)
Fix: Batched writes. Cache in Map. Flush every 30s or at 100 pending changes.

### Bug 3 — Router stores issue→repo mapping in memory (stateful)
Fix: Pure function route(). No state. No cache. No side effects. Accepts adapters param.

### Bug 4 — GitHubRepoAdapter uses execSync (blocking)
Fix: Replaced with execAsync (promisified exec). Same for ObsidianRepoAdapter and GitTransport.

### Bug 5 — ErrorCaptureLayer has no circuit breaker
Fix: Rate limiter per source (10 errors/min). Circuit breaker pattern.

### Bug 6 — Scheduler has no max depth
Fix: pops from end when queue >= 100.

### Bug 7 — Scheduler linear insert O(n) sort
Fix: Binary search insert O(log n).

### Bug 8 — Lifecycle.handleError processes same error N times
Fix: SHA-256 dedup. Same error (source + name + first 100 chars of message) within 1 min window.

### Bug 9 — Telemetry capture in Lifecycle.run re-triggers error handling
Fix: All telemetry calls wrapped in try/catch. Telemetry failures are silent.

### Bug 10 — Executor mutates original task state (side effects)
Fix: TaskRunner.execute/validate work on shallow copies. Original task is never mutated.

